index 0000000..c8f1e59
--- /dev/null
+++ b/src/npca/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,79 @@
+# Puncture-Aware NPCA for ns-3.49
+
+This patch implements *"Puncture-Aware Non-Primary Channel Access: Exploiting Preamble
+Puncturing for In-Band Spectrum Reuse in Wide-Bandwidth WLANs"* (VTC 2027-Spring) in ns-3.49
+at two levels:
+
+1. **Inside the ns-3 Wi-Fi stack** (`src/wifi`): PPDU-based (PHYLEN) NPCA following
+   IEEE P802.11bn D2.0 clause 37.18, plus the paper's puncture-aware occupancy test.
+2. **The paper's evaluation model** (`src/npca`): Algorithm 1, the 802.11be pattern tables,
+   Eq. (4)/(5), and the event-driven DCF evaluation that reproduces Fig. 2–4 and Table II.
+
+## 1. NPCA in the ns-3 Wi-Fi MAC/PHY (IEEE P802.11bn D2.0)
+
+| D2.0 | Implementation |
+|---|---|
+| 37.18.3 condition 1 (PHYLEN NPCA): inter-BSS PPDU (BSS color), NPCA_PPDU_REM_DUR − switching delay − switching back delay > 512 + NMDT×128 µs, NPCA primary channel not overlapping the channel occupied by the PPDU, intra-BSS NAV zero | `NpcaManager` (`model/uhr/npca-manager.{h,cc}`), triggered by a new `HePhy` callback at the end of HE-SIG-A/U-SIG |
+| Puncture-aware variant (paper): occupied channel = CH_BANDWIDTH minus INACTIVE_SUBCHANNELS (O = N \ P), only for valid non-OFDMA 802.11be patterns | `NpcaManager` attribute `PunctureAware` |
+| 37.18.4 rules 8), 9), 10): switch at the NPCA HE switch time, ready after the NPCA switching delay; PHY-CONFIG / CCA on the NPCA primary channel | `WifiPhy::SwitchPrimary20ForNpca()` moves only the primary 20 MHz (same RF channel, ongoing energy kept); no disassociation or MAC reset |
+| 37.18.4 rule 11): same EDCA parameter set | unchanged EDCA parameters |
+| 37.18.4 rule 12) a/b: store QSRC, CW and backoff counter; QSRC = Initial NPCA QSRC; CW = 2^QSRC(CWmin+1)−1; new backoff; QSRC resets go to Initial NPCA QSRC; NPCA_TIMER | `Txop::StartNpcaBackoff()`, `Txop::ResetCw()`/`UpdateFailedCw()`, applied by `ChannelAccessManager` when the switch completes |
+| 37.18.5: switch back at NPCA_TIMER expiry, restore QSRC, CW, backoff | `Txop::RestoreNpcaBackoff()` |
+| 37.18.4 rule 8) (second item numbered 8 in D2.0), 37.7: every frame exchange on the NPCA primary channel starts with an ICF in a non-HT (duplicate) PPDU; non-AP STA → **BSRP NTB Trigger frame**, answered by a **Multi-STA BlockAck frame in ICR context** (37.7.4, CS per 37.2.3); AP → **MU-RTS Trigger frame** answered by CTS; no RTS on NPCA | `FrameExchangeManager::SendRts()` (BSRP NTB path), `EhtFrameExchangeManager::SendNpcaIcr()`, `WifiDefaultProtectionManager` |
+| 9.3.1.22.11: BSRP NTB = individually addressed BSRP Trigger with GI And LTF Type = 3, User Info AID12 = 0, UL Length = even L-SIG LENGTH of the ICR | `CtrlTriggerHeader::SetBsrpNtb()/IsBsrpNtb()` |
+| 37.18.4 rule 10); NPCA Primary Channel Indication subfield (B37 of the Special User Info field) = 1 in Trigger frames sent on NPCA | `CtrlTriggerSpecialUserInfoField` |
+| 9.3.1.8.6 Multi-STA BlockAck: Per AID TID Info with Ack Type 1 and TID 13 = ICR context | `FrameExchangeManager::IsNpcaIcr()` |
+| 37.18.4 rule 11): PPDUs include the NPCA primary channel, exclude the occupied channels and the NPCA Disabled Subchannel Bitmap | `ChannelAccessManager::SetNpcaMaxWidth()` (largest unpunctured channel around the NPCA primary) |
+| 37.18.4 rules 14), 17): Beacon deferred until the switch back, no Probe/FILS frames on NPCA | `ChannelAccessManager::IsNpcaBlocked()` (non-QoS Txops) |
+| 9.4.2.360: UHR Operation element (Element ID Extension 151), UHR Operation Control (NPCA Enabled, NPCA Operation Parameters Present), NPCA Operation Parameters field (Figure 9-aa4), not in Beacon frames | `UhrOperation` (`model/uhr/uhr-operation.{h,cc}`), sent by `ApWifiMac`, applied by `StaWifiMac` |
+| Non-OFDMA preamble puncturing of the OBSS (needed to evaluate the paper) | `EhtConfiguration` attributes `NonOfdmaPuncturingBitmap`/`NonOfdmaPuncturingProbability`; TX spectrum with punctured subchannels; U-SIG Punctured Channel Information decoded at the receiver; SINR measured on the widest unpunctured primary channel |
+
+Rule numbers refer to the list of 37.18.4 in D2.0, which is numbered 8)-12) and then 7)-17)
+(the item numbered 8) that requires an ICF is the second one).
+
+Usage (per device of the NPCA BSS):
+
+```cpp
+auto npca = CreateObject<NpcaManager>();
+npca->SetAttribute("PunctureAware", BooleanValue(true));    // false: D2.0 NPCA
+npca->SetAttribute("NpcaPrimaryChannel", UintegerValue(2));  // AP: index within the BSS channel
+device->GetMac()->SetNpcaManager(npca);                      // STAs adopt the AP's parameters
+```
+
+Attributes: `SwitchingDelay` (100 µs), `SwitchingBackDelay` (16 µs), `MinDurationThreshold`
+(NMDT), `InitialQsrc`, `DisabledSubchannelBitmap`, `InitialControlFrame`, `FollowAp`,
+`Advertise`. Trace sources: `NpcaStart`, `NpcaEnd`, `NpcaRejected`.
+
+### Not implemented (TXOP-based NPCA or little impact on performance)
+
+- MOPLEN NPCA and condition 2 of 37.18.3 (non-HT ICF/ICR/third-PPDU sequence)
+- UHR OMP request/response (37.30) and the critical update procedure (37.31): STAs use NPCA
+  when their AP advertises it; the switching delays of the AP are used by every STA
+- MU EDCA interaction (37.18.2), DUO/DPS/EMLSR/DSO/DBE interplay, early switch back on a
+  Trigger frame with NPCA indication 0, Spatial Reuse Parameter Set settings
+- UHR PPDU formats: ns-3 has no UHR PHY, EHT PPDUs are used instead (rule 12) on PPDU formats not enforced)
+- Puncturing of the NPCA PPDU itself (an unpunctured channel around the NPCA primary is used)
+- ICF padding and LLI/DUO feedback in the ICR; MLDs (single-link devices only)
+- U-SIG puncturing information above 160 MHz and for OFDMA PPDUs
+
+## 2. Paper evaluation model (`src/npca`)
+
+| Paper | Code |
+|---|---|
+| Algorithm 1, Eq. (1)–(3) | `NpcaChannelSelector` |
+| 802.11be patterns (3/10/15), compliant family T (95 sets for U = 16) | `NpcaChannelSets` |
+| Eq. (4), Eq. (5) | `NpcaAnalyticalModel` |
+| OBSS ON/OFF, P(W), π/ppunc, q, K CSMA-coupled APs | `NpcaObssSource` |
+| DCF + NPCA (T_NPCA, T_SW, NPCA timer), fixed/informed/flexible primary, η penalty | `NpcaDcfSimulation` |
+
+## Programs
+
+| Program | What it does |
+|---|---|
+| `npca-wifi-mac` | Full-stack ns-3 Wi-Fi scenario: legacy vs D2.0 NPCA vs puncture-aware NPCA |
+| `npca_wifi_mac_sweep.py` | Sweeps ppunc for the full-stack scenario, with 95 % CIs and a plot |
+| `npca-paper-scenarios` | The paper's base and wideband scenarios (simulation or `--model=1`) |
+| `npca_reproduce.py` | Reproduces Fig. 2, 3, 4 and Table II |
+| `npca-wifi-rxvector` | RXVECTOR → (N, P) adapter demo |
+
+Tests: `./test.py -s npca` (model) and `./test.py -s wifi-npca` (Wi-Fi stack).
